From: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 19:45:00 +0200
Subject: drm/msm/dp: restore the audio jack after an unplug and plug

msm_dp_hpd_unplug_handle() signals the codec that the jack went away, but
nothing signals it back. The connect event is only sent from the enable
path, which runs on a modeset. A sink that drops HPD and comes back with
the same mode list gives userspace no reason to modeset, so the display
keeps scanning out while the jack stays reported as absent and audio is
gone until something else forces a modeset.

Signal the connect event from the plug path too, once the sink is back and
the display is still on, mirroring the disconnect the unplug path sends.

Signed-off-by: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c | 13 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -389,6 +389,9 @@ static int msm_dp_display_handle_irq_hpd(struct msm_dp_display_private *dp)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static void msm_dp_display_handle_plugged_change(struct msm_dp *msm_dp_display,
+		bool plugged);
+
 static int msm_dp_hpd_plug_handle(struct msm_dp_display_private *dp)
 {
 	int ret;
@@ -424,6 +427,16 @@ static int msm_dp_hpd_plug_handle(struct msm_dp_display_private *dp)
 
 	dp->plugged = true;
 
+	/*
+	 * The unplug that preceded this told the codec the jack went away.
+	 * Hand it back here: a sink that comes back with the same mode list
+	 * gives userspace no reason to modeset, so the enable path that
+	 * normally signals the connect event never runs and audio stays
+	 * muted for good.
+	 */
+	if (!ret && dp->msm_dp_display.power_on)
+		msm_dp_display_handle_plugged_change(&dp->msm_dp_display, true);
+
 	return ret;
 };
 
